# Git Workflow and Deployment Guide

## 1. Replace Master Branch with Prod Branch

```bash
git checkout master
git reset --hard prod
git push origin master --force
```

---

# Development and Deployment Workflow

## Flow

```text
Local Master Branch
        ↓
Push to Master Branch
        ↓
Merge Master → Prod Branch
        ↓
Pull Prod Branch on Server
        ↓
docker compose down
docker compose build
docker compose up -d
```

---

## Step 1: Switch to Master Branch (Local System)

```bash
git checkout master
```

---

## Step 2: Commit and Push Changes to Master

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "commit message"
git push origin master
```

---

## Step 3: Merge Master into Prod Branch

### Update Master Branch

```bash
git checkout master
git pull origin master
```

### Switch to Prod Branch

```bash
git checkout prod
git pull origin prod
```

### Merge Master into Prod

```bash
git merge master
```

### Commit and Push Prod Branch

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Merge master into prod"
git push origin prod
```

---

## Step 4: Deploy on Server

### Pull Latest Prod Code

```bash
git pull origin prod
```

### Rebuild and Restart Containers

```bash
docker compose down

docker compose build

docker compose up -d
```

---

# Docker Commands

## Check Running Containers

```bash
docker ps
```

## Check Container Logs

```bash
docker logs <container_id>
```

Example:

```bash
docker logs 8a1b2c3d4e5f
```

## Follow Logs in Real Time

```bash
docker logs -f <container_id>
```
